{"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is configured with one ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" per ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["PersistencePlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    writers: [","        StateWriter(keyPath: \\.items) { writes, deletes in","            for item in writes { try await db.upsert(item) }","            for id in deletes  { try await db.delete(id: id) }","        },","    ],","    debounce: .milliseconds(250),  \/\/ Default; configurable","    retry: .default                \/\/ Default; configurable",")"]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Let the persist closure ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"throw"}]},{"type":"text","text":". The flush clears its buffers before the save runs, so an error you swallow with "},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the write with it — the plugin never learns to put the batch back, and the value reaches storage only if the user happens to touch the same entity again. Throwing is what turns that into a retry. See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/RetryPolicy","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" is called automatically through the plugin lifecycle — no manual invocation needed. Register the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and pass it to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s initializer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"code":"await store.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on shutdown (","type":"text"},{"code":"scenePhase == .background","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"applicationWillTerminate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") to ensure buffered writes aren’t lost. This delegates to each registered plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Writer-Ordering","type":"heading","text":"Writer Ordering"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Writers flush sequentially in registration order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If entity B references entity A via foreign key, A’s writer "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must"}]},{"type":"text","text":" come first. Otherwise B’s upsert looks up A’s row before it exists."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"warning","name":"Warning"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register leaf entities first, aggregates last. Include a defensive fallback in upsert methods — if a referenced entity isn’t found, create it inline rather than setting the relationship to "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Skip-the-boilerplate-SwiduxPersistence","type":"heading","text":"Skip the boilerplate: `SwiduxPersistence`","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The hand-wired form above (a "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per "},{"code":"EntityStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", plus a SwiftData"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow and a DB actor you write yourself) is the low-level path. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" product turns it into a declare-and-register concern:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"annotate a domain entity with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" and the macro generates its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shadow, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toDomain()"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" converters, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistableEntity"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":" actor and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator"},{"type":"text","text":" build the container, synthesize the writers, and reuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" under the hood — exposing only a merge-based"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-hydration path so a “refresh from disk” can’t clobber unflushed writes or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"live edits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"}]},{"type":"text","text":" layers opt-in iCloud sync on top: a runtime opt-out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toggle, launch-time entitlement\/account detection, and a merge-based"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"remote-change observer. Linking it is the single signal that an app needs the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iCloud\/CloudKit\/Push entitlements."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","title":"Store","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"StateWriter","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"KeyValueStore","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"PluginHost","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins f